h $b=2.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{6}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370002 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7341349-5722-538a-a46b-c46b327387d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{x}^{2}}{225}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370004}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7341349-5722-538a-a46b-c46b327387d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{x}^{2}}{225}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370004} :answer-field/id #uuid "24b13a75-2938-57e9-b343-79d1cfb33366" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370003}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d8eb6498-fe7d-54d8-8156-e7257b7cf3ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-279127" :question/problem "![](images/92/92752dfc375c895c72d3a053a9abfd64eb64ecf9660e24b0c731e7ae9616ae7b.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=\\frac{15}{2}$ and the vertical radius has length $b=\\frac{5}{2}.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{(\\frac{15}{2})}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(\\frac{225}{4})}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\frac{25}{4})} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{4{x}^{2}}{225}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{25} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370993 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65eb186c-e14b-5e5b-b246-910f532877ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370995} {:answer/id #uuid "ba12a02d-2a23-5848-a775-1a9517753135" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370996} {:answer/id #uuid "0d8fdc06-cbcf-5c84-9ddf-a56eb7032043" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370997} {:answer/id #uuid "ceeee171-e500-5146-8d03-5a5c1bd03a64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370998} {:answer/id #uuid "4041e09f-b99a-5bc3-af3a-1a97f34bb588" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370999}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ceeee171-e500-5146-8d03-5a5c1bd03a64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370998} :answer-field/id #uuid "47ed664f-5269-578c-9dc2-0e5ea600cf72" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370994}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0bf44446-fd59-5eea-85f3-78a8c0b563be" :question/math-academy-id "q-69890" :question/problem "![](images/2a/2a7f7fc248f5582afea5240aa2f7c5f6ee421a53961640efbfae18b9c920c10d.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=4$ and the vertical radius has length $b=3.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{4}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{3}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Wide Ellipse"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087840 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087516 :question/id #uuid "af56117c-65e0-5f12-9780-7a95e6be829e" :question/math-academy-id "e-5072" :question/problem "What is the equation of the ellipse given below?\n\n![](images/3e/3e8d5ed4bf055960b50e046c0688a3c4cc69907ebb1209bb9658ac4bcba48ffe.png)" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}+\\dfrac{y^2}{b^2}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=2$ and the vertical radius has length $b=4.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{4}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "de557d1d-5f27-50e3-bcba-22b21f83267f" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088122 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97b2bb68-89cb-59c8-9356-f76f21ec7260" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{81}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293529}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97b2bb68-89cb-59c8-9356-f76f21ec7260" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{81}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293529} :answer-field/id #uuid "0415426c-2704-586e-93d9-ec13672b3656" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank}