re, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 5=10,$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 2=4.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295050 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd07ce69-7233-50e2-ade0-35bd41ecc948" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293668}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd07ce69-7233-50e2-ade0-35bd41ecc948" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293668} :answer-field/id #uuid "3506445f-e25d-5eed-9620-502f091e6d1e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294113} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e04b67f5-a816-54c3-8155-668351856ed0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293808}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e04b67f5-a816-54c3-8155-668351856ed0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293808} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c5007b9-26b4-5a76-ac1d-02ea913e3344" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294493}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f4805803-ce68-53d4-945c-e98dec710bca" :question/math-academy-id "q-279172" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=36$ and ${b}^{2}=5.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=36,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{36}=6.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=5,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{5}.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $a=6,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=\\sqrt{5}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 6=12,$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot \\sqrt{5}=2\\sqrt{5}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295051 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "846d7b07-a5c9-50d0-a790-8ca46da7e3fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293457}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "846d7b07-a5c9-50d0-a790-8ca46da7e3fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293457} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a16efb0-a185-590d-9e35-93c8dcb0f26d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294302} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c1eabad-e452-564a-88e1-27687aa4dde5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293548}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c1eabad-e452-564a-88e1-27687aa4dde5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293548} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e9f79fd-01b1-5890-b694-2f2e824a01b1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294443}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "21716470-c94c-551d-bba8-b61853f57b3c" :question/math-academy-id "q-279174" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=12$ and ${b}^{2}=9.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=12,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{12}=2\\sqrt{3}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=9,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{9}=3.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $a=2\\sqrt{3},$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=3.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3}=4\\sqrt{3},$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 3=6.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295052 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92e55227-bf1c-5ea6-85e1-7b51ef62ef62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293508}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92e55227-bf1c-5ea6-85e1-7b51ef62ef62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293508} :answer-field/id #uuid "440e9a61-755c-5fee-8379-dccea5769774" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294171} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1196f9d-7e68-5b43-b2c7-5648f5cf9901" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293622}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1196f9d-7e68-5b43-b2c7-5648f5cf9901" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293622} :answer-field/id #uuid "88343c54-e5b4-5c7e-8b0e-7c3041c31c26" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294416}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d82ddc72-1ed9-51d4-9209-e788e94b9b5b" :question/math-academy-id "q-279197" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{49}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=12$ and ${b}^{2}=49.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=12,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{12}=2\\sqrt{3}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=49,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{49}=7.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $b=7,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=2\\sqrt{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 7=14,$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3}=4\\sqrt{3}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335983 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "447870c5-0e16-591a-8300-97b1a1b53090" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$14$ and $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333622} {:answer/id #uuid "548b03ca-4238-5b00-9cb4-91def2cc07cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$14\\sqrt{2}$ and $4\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333761} {:answer/id #uuid "68381630-1c58-5c47-b731-887a1f1decb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$7$ and $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333945} {:answer/id #uuid "6aa132ec-2b5e-506f-9009-d06c05f62c18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$7$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333966} {:answer/id #uuid "f94f55ce-3720-511d-baaa-529e5639ba46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$7\\sqrt{2}$ and $2\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335173}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "447870c5-0e16-591a-8300-97b1a1b53090" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$14$ and $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333622} :answer-field/id #uuid "c27addb0-e02b-555b-8abb-615b89631ce7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field